{
  "title": "Proximal Tibia Metaphyseal Fractures - Pediatric",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4025/proximal-tibia-metaphyseal-fractures--pediatric",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 10 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Proximal Tibia Metaphyseal Fractures are fractures of the proximal tibia usually seen in children from 3 to 6 years of age. This fracture is significant for its tendency to develop a late valgus deformity, known as a Cozen's phenomenon, that must be monitored closely.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be confirmed with plain radiographs.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually closed reduction and casting in extension with a varus mold. Late valgus deformity generally resolves with observation alone.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common in children 3-6 years of age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "typically low-energy with **valgus** force across the knee creating **incomplete** fracture of proximal tibia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can also result from torsional injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "classic mechanism is a child going down a slide in the lap of an adult with leg extended",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Cozen's phenomenon**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**a late valgus deformity**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**etiology is unknown**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**can occur regardless of treatment**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "triangular shaped bone with apex anteriorly that broadens distally",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anteromedial border is subcutaneous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "blood supply",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "posterior tibial a. provides nutrient and periosteal vessels",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "nutrient vessels supply inner 2/3 of the tibial diaphysis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4025/images/screen_shot_2018-10-17_at_6.32.58_am.jpg",
                      "caption": "Pediatric tibial blood stupply"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Descriptive Classification",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "important radiographic parameters include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**complete vs incomplete**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "majority are incomplete (greenstick, torus)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**displaced vs. nondisplaced**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**associated fibula fracture**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "presence of fibula fracture suggests higher energy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "refusal to bear weight",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually minimal soft tissue swelling or deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "evaluate carefully for compartment syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4025/images/proximal%20tibia%20fracture%20cropped.jpg",
                  "caption": "shows displaced fracture of the proximal tibia"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "incomplete vs. complete fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "presence of any angulation, usually valgus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "presence of proximal fibula fracture, which may indicate a more unstable fracture pattern",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "long leg cast in extension with varus mold",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**nondisplaced fractures**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "place cast with varus mold (aim for slight overcorrection)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "casts are maintained for 4-6 weeks with serial radiographs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "weight bearing may be allowed after 2-3 weeks.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reduction, long leg cast in extension with varus mold",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**displaced fractures**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "reduction usually done under conscious sedation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "casting is same as above",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications (rare)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "inability to adequately reduce a displaced fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "secondary to soft tissue interposition",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "limited open dissection to remove interposed soft tissue",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "casting in near full extension, with or without supplemental k-wire fixation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Closed reduction**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sedation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "usually performed under conscious sedation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "an angulated greenstick fracture is completed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "cast placed in near full extension with three-point varus mold",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Open reduction**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "small medial incision over fracture site",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "removal of interposed soft tissue (periosteum, pes tendons, MCL)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "obtain an anatomic reduction under direct visualization",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may supplement with crossed k-wires",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "postoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "place into well-molded cast",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Valgus deformity (Cozen phenomenon)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4025/images/valgus%20xr.jpg",
              "caption": "shows posttraumatic valgus deformity"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**incidence**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "as high as 50%-90%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "develops 5-15 months after injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "maximum deformity observed at 12-18 months",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "risk factors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "incomplete reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "concomitant injury to proximal tibia physis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "infolded periosteum",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "injury to pes anserinus insertion, with loss of proximal tibia physeal tether, leading to asymmetric physeal growth",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "nonoperative",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**observation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "may be observed for 12-24 months with expectation of **spontaneous correction** in most cases although some patients may have a persistant valgus deformity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "parents should be counseled in advance",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "worst deformity at 18 months with an average valgus deformity of 18 degrees",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "gradually resolves by 3 years, with an average, clinically irrelevant, of 6 degrees",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "can result in S shaped tibia and persistent mechanical axis line that passed lateral to the center of the knee",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "operative",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**guided growth vs. osteotomy**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "reserved for valgus deformities >15-20 degrees near skeletal maturity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "varus producing proximal tibia and fibula osteotomy",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "medial proximal tibia epiphysiodesis",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Limb length discrepancy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "affected tibia is often longer (average 9mm)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "typically does not require intervention however parents should be counseled that this **does not resolve**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Valgus deformity** usually resolves spontaneously",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
